# =============================================================================
# MouseDroid — Docker Build Ignore
# =============================================================================
# Excludes unnecessary files from the Docker build context for faster builds.

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore

# Python caches.
#
# ``**/`` is load-bearing on every slash-free pattern here, for the same reason
# the mlflow.db block below spells it out: Docker matches each pattern against
# the whole context-relative path with Go's filepath.Match, so a bare
# ``__pycache__/`` covers ONLY the context root. It therefore excluded nothing
# at all in practice — this repo's byte-compiled output lives in ~100
# ``src/mousedroid/**/__pycache__`` directories and every one of them was being
# sent to the daemon and baked into a layer. The root-level spellings are kept
# alongside so a root-level artefact stays covered too.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
*.pyo
**/*.pyo
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.egg

# Virtual environments (``env/`` mirrors .gitignore; the 6 GB ./.venv here is
# the single biggest thing this file keeps out of the build context)
.venv/
venv/
env/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Documentation (not needed at runtime)
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Spec-driven harness — CI/agent tooling, never part of the rover runtime image.
# (HARNESS_SPEC.md / progress.md are already covered by the *.md rule above;
# the importable src/mousedroid/harness/spec.py stays in the package.)
features.yaml
features.schema.json
scripts/validations/

# Tests (installed separately in dev layer)
# tests/

# CI/CD
.github/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Temporary files
/tmp/
*.log

# 3D printing files (large CAD binaries — distributed as a GitHub Release; see the pointer README)
docs/3D_printing_files/
*.stl
*.FCStd

# Generated training artefacts (large binaries — regenerated via scripts/fetch_data.sh)
training/data/*.npz
training/data/*.pt

# Weights (large model files -- download at runtime)
weights/
models/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.tflite
*.gguf
*.bin
*.engine
*.trt
*.plan

# Isaac Sim / Omniverse generated USD (operator-local — never commit)
*.usd
*.usda
*.usdc
.nvidia-omniverse/

# Coverage / test artifacts
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
coverage.json
coverage-branch.json
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.benchmarks/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/

# Secrets / env (never bake into an image layer).
#
# Every pattern needs its ``**/`` twin — see the Python-caches note above. This
# section had the root-only spellings only, so a developer's ``config/.env`` or
# ``deployments/gcp_credentials/`` was NOT excluded, which is the one category
# here where a miss is a credential in a published layer rather than a slow
# build. (``config/.env.jetson.example`` is deliberately still included: it ends
# in ``.example``, matches neither pattern, and is a tracked placeholder.)
.env
**/.env
.env.local
**/.env.local
*.env
**/*.env
secrets.yaml
**/secrets.yaml
gcp_credentials/
**/gcp_credentials/
*.credentials.json
**/*.credentials.json

# Host-local config sidecars that would otherwise ride in through `COPY config/`
# (Dockerfile.dev) and `COPY config ./config` (docker/Dockerfile.cloud).
# config/prometheus/runtime/ is where runtime-only Prometheus SECRETS live on
# the Jetson host — its own .gitkeep says so — and it is gitignored, so it is
# exactly the local-only content that must not enter a layer. The .gitkeep is
# negated back in so the directory still exists in the image.
config/prometheus/runtime/*
!config/prometheus/runtime/.gitkeep
config/local_dual_stream_training.yaml
dev_dashboard.yaml
# Timestamped backups from operators editing YAML in place (gitignored for the
# same reason); *.bak.<stamp> needs the second pattern.
*.bak
**/*.bak
*.bak.*
**/*.bak.*

# Host-only runtime artefacts (LMDB experience, reports, training output,
# harness journal + validation trend store, MLflow tracking store).
# The LMDB patterns get the same ``**/`` twin the mlflow.db block below already
# documents — an experience store is one of the largest things on a rover host
# and was only excluded at the context root.
*.mdb
**/*.mdb
*_experience/
**/*_experience/
reports/
runs/
checkpoints/
mlruns/
# F-034: sqlite is now the default MLflow tracking backend. Mirrors the
# .gitignore entries, incl. SQLite's WAL-mode sidecars, so a developer's
# local training DB never enters the build context.
#
# Do NOT drop mlruns/ above as "legacy" — mlflow's SQLAlchemy store keeps
# its ARTIFACT root at ./mlruns even under a sqlite database, so it stays
# an active output path (verified against a real mlflow 3.x run).
#
# ``**/`` prefix, unlike .gitignore: Docker matches each pattern against
# the context-relative path with filepath.Match, so a bare ``mlflow.db``
# would cover only the context root. .gitignore's leading-slash-free
# patterns already match at any depth, hence the two files differing here
# rather than staying byte-identical.
**/mlflow.db
**/mlflow.db-wal
**/mlflow.db-shm
**/mlflow.db-journal
var/

# Claude worktrees + agent workspaces
.claude/
.serena/
.gemini/
.agents/

# Repo-hygiene surfaces (PR #151) - belt-and-suspenders: Dockerfile.jetson
# uses selective COPY so these never enter the image anyway.
.gitleaks.toml
.github/advisory_stages.yaml

# Developer entry points - thin wrappers over scripts/ with no runtime role.
Makefile

# Claude Code workforce governance (F-024) - edit-time developer tooling with no
# runtime role. Keeping it out of the build context also keeps the image free of
# a second, non-runtime pydantic/yaml consumer.
tools/claude_hooks/
